---
import LegalPage from '~/components/home/LegalPage.astro';

export const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
  description:
    'How CausewaySoft Ltd collects, uses and protects your personal information, including details you send through our contact and project enquiry forms.',
};

export const prerender = true;

/*
 * Written to describe what the site actually does (Nov 2026):
 * - contact form and project wizard emails sent via /forms/contact.php
 * - Google Analytics 4 in production (PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID)
 * - Calendly for booking calls; fonts are self-hosted
 * Review with a professional before relying on it, and keep it in sync with
 * the site (e.g. if a cookie consent banner or other tools are added).
 */
---

<LegalPage metadata={metadata} title="Privacy Policy" updated="November 16, 2026">
  <section>
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      CausewaySoft Ltd (“CausewaySoft”, “we”, “us”) is a software studio registered in Northern Ireland with company
      number NI669195. We are the data controller for the personal information described in this policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy explains what personal information we collect when you use our website or get in touch with us, why
      we use it, who we share it with, how long we keep it and the rights you have. If you have any questions, contact us
      at <a class="emailLink" href="mailto:">office@causewaysoft.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you give us:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address and message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Project enquiry form:</strong> your name and email address, your company or organisation (optional),
        the kind of project you’re interested in, your description of it, and any optional details you choose to share,
        such as budget, timing and the address of an existing website or application.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Emails, calls and meetings:</strong> anything you send us or tell us when you contact us directly.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Information collected automatically:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics:</strong> how you use our website, such as the pages you visit, how long you stay, how you
        arrived, your device and browser type and your approximate location. See section 4.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We don’t ask for special category information (such as health data), and we ask you not to include it in
      messages to us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. How we use your information and why</h2>
    <p>UK data protection law requires a lawful basis for each use of your information. Ours are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Replying to your enquiry and preparing a proposal:</strong> to take steps you’ve asked for before
        entering into a contract, and our legitimate interest in responding to people who contact us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delivering a project if you become a client:</strong> to perform our contract with you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Understanding and improving our website (analytics):</strong> your consent, given through your cookie
        choices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Keeping business and accounting records:</strong> to comply with our legal obligations.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We don’t use your information for marketing without your permission, we don’t sell it, and we don’t make
      decisions about you based solely on automated processing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use our website so we can improve it. Google Analytics sets
      cookies (such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) that can last for up to two years, and collects the
      information described in section 2. Google processes this information on our behalf.
    </p>
    <p>
      These analytics cookies are not essential for the website to work. You can block or delete cookies in your
      browser settings, or opt out of Google Analytics using the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a
      >. The website works normally without them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our website’s fonts are hosted on our own server, so loading them doesn’t send your information to a third
      party.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Who we share your information with</h2>
    <p>We only share your information with service providers who help us run our business, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>our website and email hosting providers, which store and deliver the messages you send us;</li>
      <li>Google, which provides our website analytics;</li>
      <li>
        Calendly, if you choose to book a call with us. Calendly collects the details you enter under its own privacy
        policy.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers may only use your information to provide their services to us. We may also disclose information
      if the law requires it, or to protect our rights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Some of our service providers, such as Google and Calendly, may process information outside the UK, including in
      the United States. Where they do, the transfer is protected by safeguards recognised under UK data protection
      law, such as the UK–US data bridge or the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to standard contractual
      clauses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. How long we keep your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Enquiries that don’t lead to a project:</strong> only for as long as we need them to respond and follow
        up. We review old enquiries regularly and delete those we no longer need.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clients:</strong> for the length of our working relationship, and afterwards for as long as the law
        requires us to keep business and accounting records (usually six years).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics data:</strong> according to our Google Analytics data retention settings, which allow at most
        14 months.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. How we keep your information secure</h2>
    <p>
      Our website uses an encrypted (HTTPS) connection, and access to your information is limited to the people who
      need it to respond to you or work with you. No method of sending or storing information over the internet is
      completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
      <li>ask us to delete your information;</li>
      <li>ask us to restrict how we use your information;</li>
      <li>object to us using your information on the basis of our legitimate interests;</li>
      <li>ask us to transfer your information to you or another organisation, where this applies;</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To use any of these rights, email <a class="emailLink" href="mailto:">office@causewaysoft.com</a>. There’s no
      charge, and we’ll respond within one month.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. How to complain</h2>
    <p>
      If you’re unhappy with how we’ve used your information, please contact us first so we can try to put it right.
      You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO), the UK’s data protection
      regulator: visit <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>
      or call 0303 123 1113.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>11. Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our website and services are not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time, for example when we change how our website works. Any changes will
      be posted on this page with an updated date at the top.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>13. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      For any questions about this policy or your personal information, contact CausewaySoft Ltd at
      <a class="emailLink" href="mailto:">office@causewaysoft.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
